Ham radio (App/Sources/Ham, android/ham):
- The Winlink B2F protocol, secure-login salt and LZHUF port follow wl2k-go
  (https://github.com/la5nta/wl2k-go), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2014-2017
  Martin Hebnes Pedersen (LA5NTA). Its LZHUF code is a port of JNOS 2's lzhuf.c
  (Okumura, Yoshizaki, Rikitake), licensed "use, distribute, and modify this
  program freely". Test fixtures gettysburg.txt / e.txt and their .lzh forms are
  from wl2k-go's test data.
- The FT8 decoder (App/Sources/Ham/Ft8Decoder.swift, Ft8Constants.swift and
  android/ham/.../Ft8Decoder.kt, Ft8Constants.kt) is a port of ft8_lib
  (https://github.com/kgoba/ft8_lib), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2018 Karlis
  Goba. FT8 itself is by Joe Taylor (K1JT), Steve Franke (K9AN) and Bill
  Somerville (G4WJS). The test recordings in AppTests/Fixtures/Ft8 (websdr_test4.wav,
  websdr_test6.wav) and their expected outputs come from ft8_lib's test data; the
  gen_*.wav files were made with its encoder.
- The AIS receiver (android/app/.../sdr/Ais.kt) is written from ITU-R M.1371 and
  the HDLC description. The frame bit-order and CRC conventions were checked
  against the published source of rtl-ais (GPL); no code was copied.
